+### upnp_adapters
+
+<table>
+    <tr>
+        <td>Description</td>
+        <td colspan="2">
+            Comma-separated list of network adapter names, native adapter IDs, or currently assigned IPv4
+            addresses to use for IPv4 UPnP discovery. Sunshine tries the configured candidates in order and
+            uses the first one that discovers a valid IGD. Explicit selection is strict: if none of the
+            configured adapters is available, Sunshine does not silently fall back to another interface.
+        </td>
+    </tr>
+    <tr>
+        <td>Default</td>
+        <td colspan="2">Empty. MiniUPnPc/OS automatic interface selection is used.</td>
+    </tr>
+    <tr>
+        <td>Example</td>
+        <td colspan="2">@code{}
+            upnp_adapters = Wi-Fi,Ethernet
+            @endcode</td>
+    </tr>
+</table>
+
+### upnp_adapter_blacklist
+
+<table>
+    <tr>
+        <td>Description</td>
+        <td colspan="2">
+            Optional regular expression applied to the adapter name, native ID, and description before IPv4
+            UPnP discovery. Matching adapters are excluded. The blacklist takes precedence over
+            <code>upnp_adapters</code>. If the allow-list is empty but a blacklist is configured, Sunshine
+            enumerates eligible host adapters and tries only the non-blacklisted ones.
+        </td>
+    </tr>
+    <tr>
+        <td>Default</td>
+        <td colspan="2">Empty.</td>
+    </tr>
+    <tr>
+        <td>Example</td>
+        <td colspan="2">@code{}
+            upnp_adapter_blacklist = Mihomo|Clash|Wintun
+            @endcode</td>
+    </tr>
+</table>
+
